From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] dmstyle: style EnumBand, GetDefaultBand, EnumMotif, GetMotif, EnumPattern, GetEmbellishmentLength; chord map methods E_NOTIMPL

The style object answered most enumeration methods with S_OK and nothing. Now:
- EnumBand returns the name of the index-th band (S_FALSE behind the last), GetDefaultBand the first band;
- EnumMotif only counts motif patterns (it used to list every pattern), EnumPattern lists patterns or motifs by DMUS_STYLET_* type;
- GetMotif builds a segment of the motif: length of the measures of the motif's time signature, repeats, start and loop points
  of the motif settings, a motif track and, when the motif has one, a band track with its band (DMUS_E_NOT_FOUND for a name
  which is no motif);
- GetEmbellishmentLength gives the shortest and longest pattern (in measures) of a DMUS_COMMANDT_* type at a groove level;
- GetDefaultChordMap, EnumChordMap and GetChordMap answer E_NOTIMPL (a style holds no chord maps); the FIXME on a working Load is
  now a TRACE.
